WEBVTT

00:00:03.221 --> 00:00:07.854
On the Bulk Import page, click Import to see every content type that

00:00:07.854 --> 00:00:10.421
can be imported, and pick Customer.

00:00:10.871 --> 00:00:15.370
The File Requirements card says what the file must look like.

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.936
It uses one of the enabled formats, here CSV or Excel, and its

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:22.891
very first row holds the column names.

00:00:23.343 --> 00:00:27.192
The order of the columns does not matter, and a column the type

00:00:27.192 --> 00:00:28.922
does not know is ignored.

00:00:28.922 --> 00:00:33.163
To start with the right columns, download a template in either format.

00:00:33.643 --> 00:00:39.753
The Columns Requirements table lists every column, whether it is required, and what it holds.

00:00:39.753 --> 00:00:44.443
Here the title is required, and the email, city and plan are optional.

00:00:44.927 --> 00:00:50.175
A column named ContentItemId lets a row update an item that already exists,

00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:52.507
instead of creating a new one.

